    <statement><p>Given that <m>f(-6.6) = -7.5</m> and <m>f(-6.2) = 4.2</m>, approximate
<m>f'(-6.6)</m>.</p>
<p><m>f'(-6.6) \approx</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>29.25</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



For small values of <m>h</m>,  
 <m>f'(c) \approx \frac{f(c+h) - f(c)}{h}</m>.
In this problem, <m>c = -6.6</m>, and <m>h = -6.2  + 6.6 = 0.4</m>.
<me>f'(-6.6) \approx \frac{f(-6.2) - f(-6.6)}{0.4}
  = \frac{4.2  + 7.5}{0.4}
  = 29.25.</me>


</solution>
